.policy "ruff-b029-except-with-empty-tuple" revision 2
.description "Don't write an except clause with an empty tuple as its type; it catches nothing, so name the exceptions to handle."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff B029 (flake8-bugbear): `except ():`. An empty tuple of exception types catches nothing, so the handler
// never runs. Reported at the except clause; `except* ()` and `except () as e` too.
//   except ():                 ← B029
//   except (ValueError,):      not reported (B013)
#include "python/bugbear.rr"

.violation B029(at: node) code "B029"
    "Using `except ():` with an empty tuple does not catch anything; add exceptions to handle"
    suppress ruff "B029"
B029(x) :- handler_type(x, t), kind(t, "tuple"), !handler_elt(x, _, _).
